Sorry, scientific article, excuse me.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.750
Okay, so now I kind of wanna
go more so into what clinical

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.240
and translational research is,

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.583
as compared to what we call
basic science research.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.430
So first, basic science
research is a more fundamental

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.860
and foundational research
that typically is designed

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.390
to kind of pave the way for

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.370
more applied science and medicine.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.560
And this typically involves
reducing particular problems

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:56.450
to really their simplest terms,
and then using model systems

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:57.810
in order to tackle those problems.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:00.760
So think of using different
kinds of cell types,

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.660
animal models, so you can
think of using like lab mice,

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.250
for different kinds of experiments.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:10.253
And then sometimes computer
simulations are also used.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.320
And then clinical and
translational research

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.030
is more so research that takes
from basic science research

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:22.800
and then applies that to
medical projects specifically.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.800
So it's more so designed to
impact health outcomes directly.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.270
And in the case of clinical research,

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:35.140
it typically involves human participants.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.870
And the kind of research

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.020
that we're gonna be discussing today

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:39.843
is clinical and translational.

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:44.900
So these two being both,

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:47.480
like really rigorous kinds of research

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.400
are very similar in many aspects.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:54.300
So both kind of utilize very
similar scientific research

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.520
and principles, as well as
pretty much the same kinds

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:59.173
of like research methodologies.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:03.040
And they both involve like
really rigorous collaboration

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.890
between different kinds of specialists,

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:07.790
especially in the field of
medicine, both kinds of research

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:10.973
really incorporate
specialists from both fields.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:14.710
And ultimately, they share the same goal,

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.957
which is the advancement of
knowledge, and in the field

00:05:16.957 --> 00:05:20.763
of medicine, of course, the
improvement of health outcomes.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:25.000
Okay, so going back to the paper a bit,

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.250
I kind of just wanted
to dissect this title.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.300
So again, it's the Association
of Blood Glucose Control

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.150
and Outcomes of Patients with COVID-19

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:34.110
and Pre-existing Type 2 Diabetes.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:36.460
So what this title is
basically saying is that

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:40.800
it's presenting research
about the outcomes in patients

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:44.820
that have type 2 diabetes
that contract COVID-19.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:49.320
And this word "association"
just means that the authors

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.670
are attempting to do
and compare two groups

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:55.703
and find some sort of
correlation between them.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:59.817
In this case, those those
things being COVID-19

00:05:59.817 --> 00:06:01.730
and type 2 diabetes.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:05.670
But when scientists want
to establish correlations,

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.290
the style of scientific reasoning that

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:10.960
they're typically using is
called probabilistic reasoning.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:14.040
And this is just the use
of statistical methods

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.850
in order to establish regularities,

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.300
as well as identify
patterns within data trends,

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:22.063
and then establish
significance in those trends.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:26.730
So when scientists use statistical, sorry,

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.450
probabilistic reasoning, again,

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.280
they're using statistical analysis

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:34.560
for particular data sets that they have

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.990
in order to establish significance

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:39.893
in those data trends in a rigorous way.

