to this one had already been done

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:39.840
with diabetes and the SARS epidemic,

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:41.820
which took place in 2003

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:46.120
in East Asia, as well
as throughout the world.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.670
So the authors of this
paper really wanna show

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:51.323
the same result rigorously for COVID-19.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:57.860
And lastly, diabetes is known
to affect certain populations

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:01.010
really disproportionately,
as was previously mentioned.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:04.810
And this really represents a
really serious public health

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:09.000
and a social challenge,
when we consider COVID-19,

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.020
just because of its extremely
widespread nature and

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:15.330
how quickly it spreads, and also the fact

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:17.280
that COVID-19 itself

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:20.560
also affects certain populations
